  "term": "AAMR",
  "definition": "AAMR refers to alacrima, achalasia, and impaired intellectual development syndrome, an inherited autosomal recessive condition linked to changes in the GMPPA gene. It involves reduced tear production, achalasia, and difficulties with intellectual development.",
